The source code is published so anyone can read and audit it. You may read it, build it, and run your own build
on your own Macs to check that it does what it says, for up to 14 days, the same as the free trial.

Using Satchel after that needs a licence key bought from the licensor:
- Satchel: one person, on their own Macs.
- Family: one household, up to 5 Macs.
Each licence includes one year of updates from the purchase date. The last version released in that year is
yours to keep and use for good. Renewing for another year of updates is optional.

Without written permission from the licensor you may not sell, redistribute or publish Satchel or changed
versions of it, or remove or get around its licence check.

Your data stays yours: no licence state ever makes a vault unreadable. Without a licence you can still unlock
Satchel and open and copy every item.

